---
layout: null
permalink: /news-feed.json
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
Machine-readable copy of the one news stream (_data/news.json + _posts) for the
satellite apps to fetch. One shared list — `product` classifies an item, it does
not scope it to one app. Same sortable-index trick as news.md, since Liquid
can't sort a mixed array of Documents and hashes. Served with CORS headers via
netlify.toml.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
A blurb whose `url` points at one of our posts stands in for that post — skip
the post itself so the stream doesn't show the same update twice. Match on the
post's path, not its absolute URL: `jekyll serve` rewrites site.url to
localhost, which would break an absolute-URL comparison in dev only.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign linked = "" -%}
{%- for item in site.data.news -%}
  {%- if item.url -%}{%- capture linked %}{{ linked }}{{ item.url }},{% endcapture -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign rowlist = "" -%}
{%- for post in site.posts -%}
  {%- unless linked contains post.url -%}
    {%- capture rowlist %}{{ rowlist }}{{ post.date | date: "%Y-%m-%d" }}~post~{{ forloop.index0 }},{% endcapture -%}
  {%- endunless -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- for item in site.data.news -%}
  {%- capture rowlist %}{{ rowlist }}{{ item.date }}~news~{{ forloop.index0 }},{% endcapture -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign rows = rowlist | split: "," | sort | reverse -%}
{
  "updated": "{{ site.time | date_to_xmlschema }}",
  "icons": {
    "provider": "font-awesome-6",
    "kit": "https://kit.fontawesome.com/13cabfa89d.js"
  },
  "products": {
    {%- for product in site.data.products %}
    {{ product.key | jsonify }}: {
      "name": {{ product.name | jsonify }},
      "icon": {{ product.icon | jsonify }},
      "hex": {{ product.hex | jsonify }},
      "url": "{{ product.url | absolute_url }}"
    }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {%- endfor %}
  },
  "items": [
    {%- for row in rows -%}
    {%- assign parts = row | split: "~" -%}
    {%- assign idx = parts[2] | plus: 0 -%}
    {%- if parts[1] == "post" -%}
      {%- assign entry = site.posts[idx] -%}
      {%- assign anchor = entry.slug -%}
      {%- assign body = entry.social-desc | default: entry.excerpt | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | truncatewords: 40 -%}
      {%- assign read_url = entry.url | absolute_url -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign entry = site.data.news[idx] -%}
      {%- assign anchor = entry.id -%}
      {%- assign body = entry.message -%}
      {%- assign read_url = entry.url -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%}
    Always emitted so consumers can render `item.link_text` with no fallback of
    their own. Casing is the consuming app's call — the feed does not upcase.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign read_label = entry.link_text | default: "Read more" %}
    {
      "id": {{ anchor | jsonify }},
      "date": {{ parts[0] | jsonify }},
      "product": {{ entry.product | default: "site" | jsonify }},
      "title": {{ entry.title | jsonify }},
      "message": {{ body | jsonify }},
      "url": {{ read_url | default: nil | jsonify }},
      "link_text": {{ read_label | jsonify }},
      "link": "{{ site.url }}/news/#{{ anchor }}"
    }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {%- endfor %}
  ]
}
